{"name":"Tweed","hex":"#937b56","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tweed","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A river in the United Kingdom; a river in the Scottish Borders area which for part of its length forms the border between Scotland and England. It flows into the North Sea at Berwick-upon-Tweed and Tweedmouth, England.","A municipality and community therein, in Hastings County, Ontario, Canada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tweed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tweed","blocks":[{"text":"Tweed is a rough, woollen fabric, of a soft, open, flexible texture, resembling cheviot or homespun, but more closely woven. It is usually woven with a plain weave, twill or herringbone structure. Colour effects in the yarn may be obtained by mixing dyed wool before it is spun."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Harris_tweed.jpg/330px-Harris_tweed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tweed","wikidata":"Q40601"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Tweed_making_at_the_Leach_family_woollen_mill_at_Mochdre.jpg/500px-Tweed_making_at_the_Leach_family_woollen_mill_at_Mochdre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Tweed_making_at_the_Leach_family_woollen_mill_at_Mochdre.jpg/500px-Tweed_making_at_the_Leach_family_woollen_mill_at_Mochdre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tweed making at the Leach family woollen mill at Mochdre, Powys, Wales, 1940","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATweed_making_at_the_Leach_family_woollen_mill_at_Mochdre.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Bike_in_Tweed_Stockholm_2013.jpg/500px-Bike_in_Tweed_Stockholm_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&ut